  "reply_text": "Found **one bug to fix before merging**:\n\n**[P1] `topTags` mutates the shared input array** — `src/tags.js:10`\n`tags.sort(...)` sorts in place, violating the documented non-mutation contract. `sidebar()` builds the cloud first, then reads that same array for the recent strip (`src/render.js:4–5`), so “recent” becomes ordered by popularity instead of the original input order.\n\nReproduced with `first:1, second:9, third:4`:\n- Expected recent: `first, second, third`\n- Actual recent: `second, third, first`\n- The caller’s array is also permanently reordered.\n\n**Suggested fix:** sort a copy (`[...tags].sort(...)`). Add regression tests asserting that `topTags` preserves its input and `sidebar` preserves the recent-strip order.\n\nAll 4 existing tests pass, but none catch this regression. Reviewed `main...tag-cloud` at `89f074f`; no files changed.",
